The on-screen buttons in any corner, side by side or stacked.

Brighter Pocket's settings (pocket/translation/AppKit/PocketSettings.m) let the player put the
on-screen buttons (the settings button, the handle that folds them away, and Tolkara's trackpad
and keyboard buttons) in any corner of the screen, in a row or in a column (Joe, 2026-11-13:
the bottom right, in a row, was the only place they could go).

- AKTouchControls takes vertical (the keyboard's button below the trackpad's instead of beside
  it) and keyboardFirst (the keyboard's button left or on top, for a left or top corner, so it
  stays outermost, at the corner). Both default to NO: the layout as before.
- The host's own placement (AppKit.m) is unchanged; the settings replace its constraints with
  their own, as they already replaced its trailing one.

The game is not changed. Upstream candidate.

